// Tacit for Amp: self-serve wiring. Amp has no plugin marketplace, so
// installation is two copies plus this settings merge:
//
//   1. The event plugin (the hooks.json equivalent: capture + in-flow
//      coaching):
//        cp plugins/amp/plugins/tacit.ts ~/.config/amp/plugins/
//      (or a project's .amp/plugins/ to coach one repo only). Reload with the
//      command palette's `plugins: reload`. Set TACIT_BIN in Amp's
//      environment if the tacit binary is not at {{TACIT_BIN}}.
//
//   2. The skills (Amp reads SKILL.md natively and loads them on demand by
//      name/description: no invocation syntax to learn):
//        cp -r plugins/amp/skills/* ~/.config/agents/skills/
//      (or a project's .agents/skills/). Copy: the "amp.skills.path"
//      setting may not load skills from this checkout
//      (amp 0.0.1783486870; skills placed there never loaded).
//
//   3. Merge the settings below into ~/.config/amp/settings.json (or
//      settings.jsonc: comments survive there) or a project's
//      .amp/settings.json. For an org-managed rollout, the same keys go in
//      /etc/ampcode/managed-settings.json (Linux) or
//      /Library/Application Support/ampcode/managed-settings.json (macOS),
//      which override individual settings.
//
// The plugin POSTs events straight to the local hook agent, falling back to
// `tacit hook-relay amp` (which auto-starts the agent) when nothing is
// listening; the agent idle-exits when quiet: nothing to run by hand.
{
  // The tacit_search MCP tool: the pull-based "ask path".
  "amp.mcpServers": {
    "tacit": {
      "command": "{{TACIT_BIN}}",
      "args": ["mcp"]
    }
  }
}
